Yes — the incomplete-API risk is real, but it is now explicitly handled.

### What I changed
The LLM still sees only the custom service methods, so it must use repositories for standard CRUD. I added generation-side guidance and repairs:

- standard CRUD is on repositories, not services;
- do not call a service method absent from the module;
- `read_all` takes exact field names; no `__ge`/`__le` suffixes;
- date ranges must be filtered in Python;
- date parameters may already be `datetime.date` values;
- yearly summaries use `YYYY-MM` keys;
- create preconditions run before the create, except repository-enforced FK checks;
- generated services get a `_as_date()` helper, and `datetime.date.fromisoformat(...)` calls are rewritten to accept both strings and date objects;
- generated modules import `Tuple` and `datetime`;
- the “after insert” validator now reads only the relevant clause, so `BudgetExceededException` can follow the create while `CategoryNotFoundError` is not forced after it.

