content.text:
Implemented the next verifier stage: intent schema, prompt-only intent generation, mechanical fixture planning, and end-to-end execution through the existing binder/worker.

## What changed

- `kernel/oracle/intents.py`
  - validated `TestIntent` schema;
  - source must be a prompt span;
  - rejects non-class error sentences, invalid references and misplaced CLI/app inputs;
  - downgrades `confirmed` intents when their error, date, argument or stdout is not grounded in the target clause.

- `kernel/oracle/fixtures.py`
  - topological FK setup;
  - required-field completion;
  - prompt field-spelling canonicalization;
  - synthetic method-parameter rows, e.g. `borrow_book` needs a `Member`;
  - rejects unknown actions, invented fields and cyclic required FKs;
  - records every synthetic fixture in `oracle_intent_plans.json`.

- `scripts/build_test_intents.py` — generates intents prompt-only, one clause at a time.

- `scripts/build_intent_cases.py` — turns intents into case-sidecar fixtures mechanically.

- Binder/runtime fixes:
  - generic `id` parameter binding for delete;
  - `{"ref": ...}` no longer treated as an object payload;
  - only not-found errors require a pre-seeded row;
  - relative `app.py` path resolved correctly;
  - date/datetime assertions accept ISO prompt values.

## Trial result

Across the 35 mapped-but-untested clauses:

| Result | Count |
|---|---:|
| Intents generated | 58 |
| Cases planned | 32 |
| Passed | 18 |
| Assumed-only failures | 14 |
| **Confirmed behavior findings** | **0** |
| Clauses with any passing case | 10 / 35 |
| Clauses with a confirmed passing case | 4 / 35 |

The main verifier is unchanged at **25 passed / 0 failed / 54 unbound**. Stable acceptance remains **66/66 projects, 1,023 checks, 0 stubs**.

Tests: **1,446 passed**.

Commit: `79ac653 Add intent-driven verifier fixture kernel`.

The next step is P4: merge the confirmed intent cases into the main oracle/trace, then work through the 14 assumed-only failures and the remaining 22 clauses that produced no planned case.

